WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
Take n squared plus n plus forty-one.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.470
Put in nought: forty-one.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.220
Prime.

4
00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:07.320
Put in one.

5
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:08.090
Prime.

6
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:08.570
Two.

7
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:09.750
Prime again.

8
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.700
Three, four, five: prime, prime, prime.

9
00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.910
Faster now, all the way to
thirty-nine: sixteen hundred and one.

10
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.970
Still prime.

11
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.280
Forty prime results in a row.

12
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.990
Is that enough to say it is always prime?

13
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.060
In this mission, you'll
learn what counts as a proof,

14
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:30.620
and the arrows for implies
and if and only if.

15
00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.640
You'll build proofs by deduction,
writing integers in general form,

16
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.620
like two a plus one.

17
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:41.570
And you'll meet proof by exhaustion,
splitting the possibilities into cases.

18
00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:47.490
Your mission: decide whether n squared
plus n plus forty-one is always prime.
